---
import WorkbenchLayout from "../../layouts/WorkbenchLayout.astro";
---

<WorkbenchLayout
  title="PENGO Workbench | Pengo Systems"
  description="A public reference system for inspecting AI-facing failure surfaces, structural Patterns, Lenses, and Check Input results."
  url="https://pengosystems.com/workbench/"
  active=""
>
  <article class="wb-content wb-template">
    <p class="wb-type-label">Workbench Home</p>
    <h1>PENGO Workbench</h1>
    <p class="wb-lede">
      Inspect AI-facing failures by separating visible symptoms, missing input structure, structural Patterns, and diagnostic Lenses.
    </p>

    <section class="wb-section">
      <h2>Start with the job</h2>

      <div class="wb-row-list">
        <a class="wb-row" href="/workbench/search/">
          <p class="wb-row-meta">Search</p>
          <h2>Search the Workbench</h2>
          <p>Find Issues, AI-Adjacent Issues, Patterns, Lenses, codes, and related reference pages.</p>
        </a>

        <a class="wb-row" href="/workbench/check-input/">
          <p class="wb-row-meta">Input inspection</p>
          <h2>Check an AI Ask</h2>
          <p>Use Check Input to surface missing, unclear, ambiguous, unstated, conflicting, incomplete, or implied parts of an ask.</p>
        </a>

        <a class="wb-row" href="/workbench/explore-results/">
          <p class="wb-row-meta">Result mapping</p>
          <h2>Explore Check Input Results</h2>
          <p>Map controlled Check Input gaps into inspection lanes and related Workbench references.</p>
        </a>

        <a class="wb-row" href="/workbench/issues/">
          <p class="wb-row-meta">Browse</p>
          <h2>Browse visible failure surfaces</h2>
          <p>Browse common AI-era failure symptoms and the structural Patterns they may surface.</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="wb-section">
      <h2>Reference Areas</h2>

      <div class="wb-row-list">
        <a class="wb-row" href="/workbench/issues/">
          <p class="wb-row-meta">Issues</p>
          <h2>Issues</h2>
          <p>Visible failure surfaces users may experience or search for.</p>
        </a>

        <a class="wb-row" href="/workbench/ai-adj-issues/">
          <p class="wb-row-meta">AI-Adjacent Issues</p>
          <h2>AI-Adjacent Issues</h2>
          <p>Problems users may experience as AI failures, but which may involve tools, apps, permissions, configuration, or integrations.</p>
        </a>

        <a class="wb-row" href="/workbench/patterns/">
          <p class="wb-row-meta">Patterns</p>
          <h2>Patterns</h2>
          <p>Canonical structural forms used to inspect why a visible failure surface may appear.</p>
        </a>

        <a class="wb-row" href="/workbench/lenses/">
          <p class="wb-row-meta">Lenses</p>
          <h2>Lenses</h2>
          <p>Diagnostic views for inspecting structure without treating the reference as a final diagnosis.</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="wb-reading-section">
      <h2>Boundary</h2>
      <p>
        Workbench references help inspect structure. They do not prove causality,
        diagnose a model, validate a prompt, score a system, or replace human review.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</WorkbenchLayout>
